1
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:38,079
What is that serious issue
of you and Sir Norberto?

2
00:00:38,163 --> 00:00:40,749
<i>Remember when I said</i>
<i>that Senator Quintin keeps pushing</i>

3
00:00:40,832 --> 00:00:43,460
to involve Mikoy and Chiara
in the agency again?

4
00:00:49,799 --> 00:00:50,967
Okay.

5
00:00:52,343 --> 00:00:54,012
Donabel and Viktor are being held
in a maximum-security facility.

6
00:00:54,095 --> 00:00:56,431
Maybe we could ask the judge for a favor,

7
00:00:56,514 --> 00:00:58,558
<i>so they can at least attend</i>
<i>their daughter's wedding.</i>

8
00:00:58,641 --> 00:01:00,393
What you're asking for, Mikoy,
won't be easy.

9
00:01:00,477 --> 00:01:01,895
But it's not impossible, is it?

10
00:01:01,978 --> 00:01:03,480
I'll see what I can do.

11
00:01:03,563 --> 00:01:04,522
Thank you, Alex.

12
00:01:12,489 --> 00:01:13,740
No matter what happened,

13
00:01:13,823 --> 00:01:16,326
no matter what our families
have been through,

14
00:01:16,409 --> 00:01:18,369
we're one family now.

15
00:01:18,453 --> 00:01:20,747
I know who I want to invite.

16
00:01:22,957 --> 00:01:25,960
That's great. Anyone's fine, sweetheart.

17
00:01:26,044 --> 00:01:27,003
As long as it's your choice.

18
00:01:57,659 --> 00:02:00,995
If you're calling to borrow money,
I don't have any.

19
00:02:01,079 --> 00:02:03,081
Mikoy and I are getting married.

20
00:02:03,164 --> 00:02:04,290
Oh.

21
00:02:26,604 --> 00:02:27,856
Come on.

22
00:02:28,356 --> 00:02:29,941
It's embarrassing.

23
00:02:30,024 --> 00:02:32,235
There won't be anyone sitting
on the bride's side.

24
00:02:32,819 --> 00:02:35,280
<i>What if the photographer calls</i>

25
00:02:35,905 --> 00:02:38,324
<i>for the bride's friends and family?</i>

26
00:02:38,408 --> 00:02:40,827
And no one comes forward for the picture?

27
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:41,953
Not even one.

28
00:02:47,792 --> 00:02:49,127
Are you coming or not?

29
00:02:57,427 --> 00:02:58,636
<i>Now look at you.</i>

30
00:03:01,556 --> 00:03:03,349
You're so stubborn.

31
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:05,059
If only you'd listened to me.

32
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:08,646
So, are you coming or not?

33
00:03:18,406 --> 00:03:21,534
You know, I wasn't expecting much anyway.

34
00:03:23,953 --> 00:03:25,622
I even tried to invite you.

35
00:03:26,122 --> 00:03:27,999
If you don't want to come, then don't.

36
00:03:46,017 --> 00:03:49,896
- I'll think about it.
- Yes, I've heard that before.

37
00:03:51,731 --> 00:03:52,690
Bro.

38
00:03:53,316 --> 00:03:54,567
Come on.

39
00:03:54,651 --> 00:03:57,862
- At least give me a cut of the profits.
- It's not about the money.

40
00:03:57,946 --> 00:04:01,783
Besides, Chiara would have to agree
to livestream our wedding.

41
00:04:02,283 --> 00:04:04,619
And isn't that kind of weird?

42
00:04:05,203 --> 00:04:06,537
I mean,

43
00:04:06,621 --> 00:04:10,083
Chiara and I are just ordinary people,
and we'd livestream our wedding?

44
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:11,834
Right?

45
00:04:11,918 --> 00:04:16,673
You know, Mikoy,
there are a lot of advantages to it.

46
00:04:17,423 --> 00:04:20,718
First of all, not everyone
is invited to your wedding.

47
00:04:20,802 --> 00:04:24,055
Second, not everyone can make it.

48
00:04:24,555 --> 00:04:26,724
That's why a livestream
would be a great idea.

49
00:04:26,808 --> 00:04:30,645
So they can still be part
of your special day.

50
00:04:30,728 --> 00:04:31,688
Right?

51
00:04:34,357 --> 00:04:35,566
You do have a point.

52
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:37,318
- See?
- But the thing is,

53
00:04:38,361 --> 00:04:41,656
our situation is a bit complicated.

54
00:04:41,739 --> 00:04:44,909
You know Chiara and I.
As much as possible,

55
00:04:44,993 --> 00:04:47,870
we want to keep a low profile
because, well,

56
00:04:47,954 --> 00:04:49,580
we might attract some haters.

57
00:04:50,456 --> 00:04:51,833
Haters?

58
00:04:55,044 --> 00:04:57,714
You mean people who hate the Valtrovis?

59
00:04:59,924 --> 00:05:00,842
Bro.

60
00:05:01,718 --> 00:05:05,096
One Google search
is enough for them to know

61
00:05:05,179 --> 00:05:07,765
that Chiara is the daughter
of Mr. and Mrs. Valtrovi,

62
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:11,853
who are now in prison
for allegedly running a crime syndicate.

63
00:05:12,395 --> 00:05:19,152
And a lot of people online believe
she was involved in her parents' business.

64
00:05:20,611 --> 00:05:22,405
They even say she should be in prison too.

65
00:05:22,488 --> 00:05:23,781
And that's not all, bro.

66
00:05:24,866 --> 00:05:27,827
She's also part of all these
online conspiracy theories

67
00:05:27,910 --> 00:05:32,248
claiming the government is covering up
what really happened.

68
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:34,751
Really?

69
00:05:34,834 --> 00:05:36,586
That's what people are saying about her?

70
00:05:36,669 --> 00:05:37,962
That's not even half of it.

71
00:05:38,046 --> 00:05:39,172
There's more.

72
00:05:39,672 --> 00:05:42,759
People even comment on my vlogs
whenever they see you two.

73
00:05:42,842 --> 00:05:44,844
And they say you, Bro Mikoy…

74
00:05:44,927 --> 00:05:45,928
You.

75
00:05:46,471 --> 00:05:50,391
You're the one who knows where
the Yamashita treasure is hidden.

76
00:05:53,311 --> 00:05:55,271
- Yes.
- Why me?

77
00:05:56,105 --> 00:05:59,567
I didn't even know
people still talked about Yamashita.

78
00:06:00,693 --> 00:06:03,321
And they also think

79
00:06:05,031 --> 00:06:06,365
you're a vampire.

80
00:06:08,576 --> 00:06:10,078
What happened?

81
00:06:10,787 --> 00:06:13,372
That's getting way out of hand.

82
00:06:13,456 --> 00:06:15,917
First it was the Yamashita treasure.
Now I'm a vampire?

83
00:06:16,542 --> 00:06:18,127
That doesn't even make sense.

84
00:06:18,878 --> 00:06:21,422
Just delete all those hateful comments.

85
00:06:21,506 --> 00:06:23,091
They're all fake news.

86
00:06:24,884 --> 00:06:27,637
Bro Mikoy, these days,

87
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:29,764
people can't tell fake from real anymore.

88
00:06:30,348 --> 00:06:31,349
True.

89
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:37,313
Engagement is what gets monetized.
That's where the money is.

90
00:06:37,814 --> 00:06:39,482
That's where the money is.

91
00:06:39,565 --> 00:06:42,902
You could even pretend to be homeless
for a social experiment.

92
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:45,780
You can do pranks, be whoever you want.

93
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:49,909
You can do just about anything
to drive engagement because

94
00:06:50,618 --> 00:06:53,371
engagement is the new oil.

95
00:06:54,455 --> 00:06:55,915
You and Chiara…

96
00:07:02,672 --> 00:07:04,549
You've got even more than the Middle East.

97
00:07:04,632 --> 00:07:06,884
You just don't have
a social media presence.

98
00:07:06,968 --> 00:07:08,678
You don't have a social media manager.

99
00:07:09,595 --> 00:07:12,640
People are already talking about you,
whispering about you.

100
00:07:15,893 --> 00:07:19,397
Now is the perfect time
to introduce you online.

101
00:07:20,189 --> 00:07:25,528
That's why I want to officially
launch your love team

102
00:07:25,611 --> 00:07:27,321
on your wedding day.

103
00:07:28,573 --> 00:07:29,907
Right?

104
00:07:31,951 --> 00:07:33,536
Look at you smiling.

105
00:07:33,619 --> 00:07:35,329
What? You agree now.

106
00:07:38,875 --> 00:07:39,959
You know what?

107
00:07:40,042 --> 00:07:41,127
What?

108
00:07:41,210 --> 00:07:43,796
Let's see if you can
convince Chiara first.

109
00:07:45,465 --> 00:07:47,341
- We'll see.
- We'll see.

110
00:07:48,426 --> 00:07:49,886
Come on, Mikoy.

111
00:07:49,969 --> 00:07:52,805
With your undying love and support,

112
00:07:52,889 --> 00:07:56,267
I think we can convince Chiara.

113
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:02,773
All right, then. We'll see!

114
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:04,901
We'll see. Cheers.

115
00:08:17,288 --> 00:08:18,456
How's it going, Bok?

116
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:22,251
How did things go between Alex and Mikoy?

117
00:08:23,669 --> 00:08:24,754
It went well.

118
00:08:25,505 --> 00:08:26,881
I told him

119
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:29,759
I'm okay with being
Chiara's maid of honor.

120
00:08:35,014 --> 00:08:37,975
Have you ever been a maid of honor before?

121
00:08:41,729 --> 00:08:43,940
Okay. Well, here's the thing, Bok.

122
00:08:49,111 --> 00:08:54,617
You'll help Chiara with every decision
leading up to the wedding.

123
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:56,202
All the way until the big day.

124
00:08:56,786 --> 00:08:58,704
You'll go with her to dress fittings,

125
00:08:58,788 --> 00:09:01,290
food tastings, and cake tastings.

126
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:02,583
Then,

127
00:09:03,167 --> 00:09:06,462
when the wedding day finally comes,

128
00:09:06,546 --> 00:09:10,883
you'll also have to speak,
give a speech, for her and her wedding,

129
00:09:11,717 --> 00:09:17,265
and you'll be the number one witness
signing the marriage certificate.

130
00:09:17,348 --> 00:09:18,975
And ultimately,

131
00:09:19,058 --> 00:09:20,434
you're the sacrifice.

132
00:09:21,018 --> 00:09:23,271
You're the one who isn't allowed
to outshine the bride,

133
00:09:23,354 --> 00:09:25,022
so her beauty stands out.

134
00:09:30,319 --> 00:09:31,904
She's not afraid of anyone.

135
00:09:32,655 --> 00:09:35,408
She's confident enough to hold her own.

136
00:09:35,491 --> 00:09:38,744
Then that's perfect. Perfect.

137
00:09:38,828 --> 00:09:41,455
You're the perfect
maid of honor for Chiara.

138
00:09:42,039 --> 00:09:43,749
You may not be super close,

139
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:46,335
and your friendship may not be

140
00:09:46,419 --> 00:09:49,130
what people would consider
traditional or perfect,

141
00:09:50,089 --> 00:09:51,966
but from everything you've said,

142
00:09:52,049 --> 00:09:53,634
you already know her so well.

143
00:09:56,053 --> 00:10:00,391
And I think Carlota and Cocoy's
SWOT analysis was right.

144
00:10:03,102 --> 00:10:07,106
Maybe this is an opportunity
for me to get closer to Chiara.

145
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:09,358
So I can keep an eye on her.

146
00:10:10,651 --> 00:10:14,572
And make sure she doesn't
go back to her old ways.

147
00:10:17,658 --> 00:10:20,578
Or maybe a better question is,

148
00:10:20,661 --> 00:10:21,912
will you be okay?

149
00:10:27,376 --> 00:10:28,836
Of course, Bok!

150
00:10:29,378 --> 00:10:30,338
When am I not?

151
00:10:30,421 --> 00:10:31,922
Come on.

152
00:10:32,006 --> 00:10:33,299
You have nothing to worry about.

153
00:10:56,238 --> 00:10:58,824
You can do this! You can do this!

154
00:10:59,408 --> 00:11:00,826
You can do this.

155
00:11:02,203 --> 00:11:05,706
You asked for this! You idiot!

156
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:28,604
You can't really blame her,
after everything she's been through

157
00:11:29,313 --> 00:11:30,689
on that complicated mission.

158
00:11:30,773 --> 00:11:34,819
But I'm afraid she might be
heading toward burnout.

159
00:11:41,242 --> 00:11:44,578
She can handle anything
life throws at her.

160
00:11:46,997 --> 00:11:50,960
That reminds me of the saying,
if someone throws a stone at you,

161
00:11:51,710 --> 00:11:54,130
throw back a loaf of bread
with peanut butter.

162
00:11:54,213 --> 00:11:56,465
That way, you won't get
stressed or burned out.

163
00:12:06,642 --> 00:12:09,562
If someone throws a stone at you,

164
00:12:09,645 --> 00:12:12,148
build a stone house with it.

165
00:12:12,231 --> 00:12:17,153
But what's the point of a stone house
if an owl is the one living in it?

166
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:23,451
Owl.

167
00:12:25,536 --> 00:12:28,247
Anyway, compadre…

168
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:33,669
Is it true you've been talking
to Agent Alex

169
00:12:34,587 --> 00:12:39,884
about recruiting Mikoy
and Chiara into the agency?

170
00:12:59,945 --> 00:13:01,197
<i>Engagement, engagement</i>

171
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:03,532
<i>The new currency, a simple comment</i>

172
00:13:03,616 --> 00:13:04,867
<i>It's got value, it's got power</i>

173
00:13:04,950 --> 00:13:06,952
<i>Like, share, react, don't be shy</i>

174
00:13:07,036 --> 00:13:09,413
<i>Every click you make is another milk tea</i>

175
00:13:09,497 --> 00:13:11,957
<i>Comment "sana all" or just "first"</i>

176
00:13:12,041 --> 00:13:13,751
<i>As long as there's engagement</i>
<i>It can be monetized</i>

177
00:13:13,834 --> 00:13:15,085
<i>Bang!</i>

178
00:13:15,169 --> 00:13:16,837
<i>Bang!</i>

179
00:13:16,921 --> 00:13:18,380
<i>He dodged it</i>

180
00:13:18,464 --> 00:13:20,216
<i>Still hit the old man</i>

181
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:25,429
So? Chiara, have you decided?

182
00:13:27,014 --> 00:13:29,433
Will you let us livestream
your wedding with Mikoy?

183
00:13:34,647 --> 00:13:35,856
I told you.

184
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:38,150
It's hard to say no to this goofball.

185
00:13:38,692 --> 00:13:39,568
So?

186
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:42,363
What's your decision, Chiara?

187
00:13:50,037 --> 00:13:51,622
I'm a little worried.

188
00:13:53,457 --> 00:13:54,708
Worried? About what?

189
00:13:55,543 --> 00:13:56,377
About you.

190
00:13:57,753 --> 00:13:59,338
Me? Why?

191
00:14:00,089 --> 00:14:03,467
I'm worried you're living
just for engagement now.

192
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:07,471
That you'll always start putting
other people's wants first

193
00:14:07,555 --> 00:14:08,973
before being yourself.

194
00:14:09,056 --> 00:14:10,266
Hey, no.

195
00:14:10,808 --> 00:14:11,934
I'm only different online.

196
00:14:12,726 --> 00:14:14,687
But when I'm with you guys,

197
00:14:15,187 --> 00:14:16,647
I'm my real self.

198
00:14:16,730 --> 00:14:18,107
I'm just Rahmboy.

199
00:14:19,316 --> 00:14:20,609
Just Rahmboy.

200
00:14:20,693 --> 00:14:21,735
Rahmboy!

201
00:14:21,819 --> 00:14:25,406
Well, if that's the case,
then that's good.

202
00:14:26,782 --> 00:14:28,868
I just don't want you to end up like me.

203
00:14:29,618 --> 00:14:31,453
My whole life,

204
00:14:31,537 --> 00:14:33,622
I lived for other people.

205
00:14:34,206 --> 00:14:36,876
I thought that's where I'd find meaning.

206
00:14:41,463 --> 00:14:43,924
It made me feel like
I mattered to other people.

207
00:14:45,134 --> 00:14:47,928
But slowly, I realized

208
00:14:49,263 --> 00:14:51,974
I became someone I didn't want to be.

209
00:14:52,975 --> 00:14:55,436
Until I started resenting myself.

210
00:14:56,103 --> 00:14:58,022
Good thing I met Mikoy.

211
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:02,359
When I met Mikoy for the first time,

212
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:06,030
I finally thought about
what I truly wanted for myself.

213
00:15:11,327 --> 00:15:13,704
I feel so lucky that I was given
the chance,

214
00:15:13,787 --> 00:15:15,748
not only to be true to myself,

215
00:15:15,831 --> 00:15:17,625
but to truly be happy.

216
00:15:18,751 --> 00:15:21,420
So you're right.

217
00:15:22,129 --> 00:15:24,381
Engagement can be lucrative,

218
00:15:24,965 --> 00:15:28,344
as long as you don't
lose yourself in the process.

219
00:15:29,762 --> 00:15:34,141
Don't put other people first,
don't live your life for others,

220
00:15:34,224 --> 00:15:36,685
and genuinely love yourself.

221
00:15:41,065 --> 00:15:43,400
You can livestream my wedding.

222
00:15:43,484 --> 00:15:44,860
There we go!

223
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:47,071
- It's settled.
- Way to go, Rahmboy!

224
00:15:47,154 --> 00:15:48,781
- It's settled.
- That's more like it!

225
00:15:50,282 --> 00:15:52,201
You actually convinced Chiara.

226
00:15:57,247 --> 00:15:58,332
Wait.

227
00:15:58,415 --> 00:15:59,667
What is it?

228
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:18,227
Ask Sianong.

229
00:16:20,437 --> 00:16:25,609
Those are the habits
of highly effective people.

230
00:16:27,861 --> 00:16:34,243
But still, I don't think it's right
for you to be talking to my agents

231
00:16:34,743 --> 00:16:36,161
behind my back.

232
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:41,458
Why? You seem upset.

233
00:16:42,167 --> 00:16:43,460
What happened?

234
00:16:45,421 --> 00:16:46,755
Chiara.

235
00:16:47,506 --> 00:16:48,424
Mikoy.

236
00:16:50,592 --> 00:16:51,885
What?

237
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:55,639
I think…

238
00:16:57,307 --> 00:16:58,851
it's better if there's no livestream.

239
00:16:59,601 --> 00:17:00,436
Oh, no.

240
00:17:00,519 --> 00:17:02,479
This kid's gone crazy.

241
00:17:02,563 --> 00:17:04,356
Why do you keep changing your mind?

242
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:05,649
Exactly.

243
00:17:05,733 --> 00:17:08,569
Honey, that's just how Gen Z is.

244
00:17:09,528 --> 00:17:10,863
Just let it go.

245
00:17:13,365 --> 00:17:14,658
What I mean is,

246
00:17:14,742 --> 00:17:16,827
while I was listening,

247
00:17:17,411 --> 00:17:21,707
I realized just how special
your love really is.

248
00:17:25,836 --> 00:17:28,797
And, of course, I don't want it
to be ruined

249
00:17:28,881 --> 00:17:33,177
by some attention-seeking hater
who'll just say,

250
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:34,595
"Your food wasn't even good."

251
00:17:35,179 --> 00:17:36,680
"Their own parents don't love them."

252
00:17:36,764 --> 00:17:38,307
"No one loves them."

253
00:17:38,390 --> 00:17:39,349
Right?

254
00:17:51,153 --> 00:17:52,988
<i>Engagement, engagement</i>
<i>Don't turn it into a trap</i>

255
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:55,449
<i>Clickbait and fake tears</i>
<i>Shouldn't be your whole world</i>

256
00:17:55,532 --> 00:17:57,451
<i>The algorithm loves anger and drama</i>

257
00:17:57,534 --> 00:18:00,120
<i>The truth gets left behind</i>
<i>When clout takes center stage</i>

258
00:18:00,204 --> 00:18:02,581
<i>Before you react, take a moment to think</i>

259
00:18:02,664 --> 00:18:05,209
<i>Not every engagement should be monetized</i>

260
00:18:06,168 --> 00:18:07,377
<i>Our food is delicious</i>

261
00:18:07,461 --> 00:18:10,047
<i>Laing, loaded with coconut milk!</i>

262
00:18:10,130 --> 00:18:12,091
<i>Bicol Express, rich in coconut milk!</i>

263
00:18:15,969 --> 00:18:17,346
<i>Coconut milk!</i>

264
00:19:00,973 --> 00:19:02,432
You're right.

265
00:19:03,350 --> 00:19:04,643
These days,

266
00:19:05,269 --> 00:19:08,730
politicians are starting to look
like the bad guys in people's eyes.

267
00:19:09,731 --> 00:19:11,233
So I promise

268
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:13,402
it won't happen again.

269
00:19:13,485 --> 00:19:14,820
May lightning strike me.

270
00:19:15,404 --> 00:19:17,072
May I be pierced by a spear.

271
00:19:17,156 --> 00:19:18,740
Or even be eaten by a crocodile.

272
00:19:27,332 --> 00:19:29,334
By the way,

273
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:32,671
I have a really good knock-knock joke.

274
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:37,551
I know it's going to go viral.

275
00:19:37,634 --> 00:19:39,178
I dreamed about it.

276
00:19:46,935 --> 00:19:49,938
…in the garden!

277
00:19:58,530 --> 00:20:00,616
That's definitely going viral!

278
00:20:02,409 --> 00:20:03,994
Hey, that's a foul!

279
00:20:04,077 --> 00:20:06,496
I'll be back later! We'll make content.

280
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:07,789
I'll just be over there.

281
00:20:16,757 --> 00:20:17,841
Hello, Mom.

282
00:20:17,925 --> 00:20:19,092
What's wrong?

283
00:21:37,921 --> 00:21:38,922
Chiara?

284
00:21:49,349 --> 00:21:51,727
According to an old belief,

285
00:21:51,810 --> 00:21:56,648
at the stroke of midnight,
a mysterious power drips from the heart

286
00:21:56,732 --> 00:21:58,734
of a banana tree.

287
00:21:58,817 --> 00:21:59,943
Come with me.

288
00:22:00,027 --> 00:22:03,322
Let's go, let's go.

289
00:22:11,872 --> 00:22:12,789
Nothing.

290
00:22:13,999 --> 00:22:16,418
Well, that didn't exactly work out, but…

291
00:22:17,169 --> 00:22:19,421
we're survivors, so we have a Plan B.

292
00:22:19,504 --> 00:22:22,632
B for "bukas".
We'll try again tomorrow, okay?

293
00:22:22,716 --> 00:22:24,968
See you, Rahmboys and Rahmgirls.

294
00:22:25,052 --> 00:22:26,219
Love you all.

295
00:22:30,015 --> 00:22:33,810
I thought it was some creep
out here in the middle of the night.

296
00:22:33,894 --> 00:22:38,315
Ever since then,
that kid has been sticking with us.

297
00:22:38,398 --> 00:22:39,858
Yes.

298
00:22:40,442 --> 00:22:41,985
Doesn't he have parents?

299
00:22:42,069 --> 00:22:43,028
Hey, where are you going?

300
00:22:43,111 --> 00:22:46,865
He does. I think he mentioned
his mom works overseas.

301
00:22:47,574 --> 00:22:49,785
The problem is, his parents are separated,

302
00:22:49,868 --> 00:22:51,578
so he's all alone now.

303
00:22:51,661 --> 00:22:53,747
He has no one with him.

304
00:22:54,247 --> 00:22:55,832
Well, he used to.

305
00:22:55,916 --> 00:22:59,419
But apparently, someone kept stealing
the money his mom sent him.

306
00:23:00,754 --> 00:23:01,588
Poor kid.

307
00:23:01,671 --> 00:23:04,299
Maybe that's why he's so attached to us.

308
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:08,053
Looks like he doesn't get along
with his relatives either.

309
00:23:08,136 --> 00:23:09,346
Hey, where are you going?

310
00:23:11,723 --> 00:23:12,766
Poor kid.

311
00:23:12,849 --> 00:23:14,351
Isn't he in school?

312
00:23:15,102 --> 00:23:16,603
He just graduated.

313
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:19,898
But he's really more
into vlogging these days.

314
00:23:19,981 --> 00:23:23,902
You know, he's a liver vlogger!

315
00:23:25,946 --> 00:23:27,739
You two seem pretty close.

316
00:23:29,199 --> 00:23:30,367
He reminds you of all the fun

317
00:23:30,450 --> 00:23:32,327
you had with your brother
Angelito, doesn't he?

318
00:23:35,122 --> 00:23:37,374
Of course. I really miss that.

319
00:23:38,125 --> 00:23:41,253
But I'm also happy that Rahmboy's around.

320
00:23:42,379 --> 00:23:45,257
He reminds me of the life
Angelito and I had in Cebu.

321
00:23:45,757 --> 00:23:49,094
You know, back when
everything was so simple.

322
00:23:49,719 --> 00:23:51,388
Just imagine, sweetheart.
Back then, all I ever wanted

323
00:23:51,471 --> 00:23:54,599
was for him to finish school
and become an engineer.

324
00:23:54,683 --> 00:23:55,851
That was all.

325
00:24:07,154 --> 00:24:08,697
Norberto.

326
00:24:08,780 --> 00:24:11,950
I heard you're planning to report
Quintin to the Ombudsman.

327
00:24:16,621 --> 00:24:20,417
Because he diverted the agency's budget.

328
00:24:36,808 --> 00:24:41,188
Then how do you explain
the evidence linking you

329
00:24:42,355 --> 00:24:44,149
to the Sinigang Cartel?

330
00:24:45,025 --> 00:24:48,653
Are you sure you're not going
to investigate Senator Quintin?

331
00:24:48,737 --> 00:24:50,238
Norberto.

332
00:24:50,322 --> 00:24:53,742
One thing I've learned
through all my years in office is,

333
00:24:53,825 --> 00:24:55,577
keep your friends close,

334
00:24:56,995 --> 00:24:58,914
but keep your enemies closer.

335
00:25:01,249 --> 00:25:02,542
And you still forgot it!

336
00:25:02,626 --> 00:25:04,794
Why did you forget it?

337
00:25:08,673 --> 00:25:11,343
I told you I needed the groceries!

338
00:25:15,597 --> 00:25:18,767
Looks like we can't count
on our friend anymore.

339
00:25:30,278 --> 00:25:33,531
I swear, all day long,
I kept reminding myself to buy groceries.

340
00:25:33,615 --> 00:25:35,200
We can deal with that later.

341
00:25:35,283 --> 00:25:38,036
I just wanted to tell you
that you have a visitor.
